{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1101921-precursors-to-the-gentry","id":1101921,"title":"Precursors to the Gentry","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-09T04:37:37-07:00","id":1101921,"title":"Precursors to the Gentry","content":"In Beast the Primordial it has an off-hand comment that there were &quot;monstrous precursors to the Gentry&quot;. What sort of entities do people think of which could fit being such ancient entities of the Wyrd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T04:52:39-07:00","id":1101926,"title":"","content":"Primordial dream seems precursorial to Arcadia. One the Lizard Brain subconscious, the other a higher realm of unconsciousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T05:05:43-07:00","id":1101930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1101921-precursors-to-the-gentry?p=1101926#post1101926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordial dream seems precursorial to Arcadia. One the Lizard Brain subconscious, the other a higher realm of unconsciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it was talking about them wasn't saying they were Primordial Dream phenomena, it listed them along with entities like The Original Vampires and Father Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T06:31:17-07:00","id":1101949,"title":"","content":"Primordial manifestation of Wyrd, unable to draw on human facades and &quot;civilized&quot; fears for their stories and roles. Which is interesting because both the Primordial Dream and the Wyrd are shaped and granted strength by stories and dreams, though in different ways.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, it's a bit of ying-yang thing, where the Primordial Dream is the savage, lively and istinctive lens for those stories as elaborated by the shared perception of the human mind while the Wyrd is colder, more ordered and structured lens which elaborates the same stories in a more alien and detached way. Which I admit is not a perfect analogy, since the Gentry and Changeling have a lot to say about passions and emotions. Then again, we're talking about stories and fears, which in turn means we're talking about humanity and emotions, so that might still be a useful way to look at things, if used with moderation.<br /> <br /> We do know the Primordial Dream was different when the human race was young, in a way more indifferent towards mankind. I can imagine that when the conventions, stories and dreams that shape the modern Hedge and Arcadia were not a thing, the things that lived there were...not pretty. Even more monstrous and alien to mankind, if possible. I'm thinking about something older than Homo Sapiens, the kind of thing that might be a soul-stealing horror for prehistoric times. I admit the image of &quot;Wyld Hunts&quot; made of waves of thorns and teeth is kinda cool.<br /> <br /> All in all, an interesting topic to think about. Which is perhaps not relevant to modern Changeling, but you can always go for the classic &quot;monster older than our monsters that awakens&quot; storyline, if that fits your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-09-2017, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T08:20:11-07:00","id":1101992,"title":"","content":"My bet? The Huntsmen. Or at least, the poor souls the Huntsmen gathered in their &quot;Wild Hunts&quot;<br /> <br /> (in my head canon, the Huntsmen once were the ancient form of the Wyrd, horned kings and queens who lived in their hunts, treating mankind as their prey- taking the sick and the dying, the young and the old as their own. One day, soon after Father Wolf's death at the late Neolithic, humanity has started to tell new stories in order to protect themselves from the hunters- the Gentry. One community at a time, the mysterious new Fae revealed themselves before mankind, offering pledges in exchange for protection. They became the new gods of the People- the so called &quot;Lost Pantheon&quot;. They made a pact with the first people- that they will protect them from the hunters of the wilderness, and in exchange they will tell stories about them, to define and worship them. Thanks to that combined effort, the Gentry conquered the Huntsmen and made them into their own... only for humanity to discover that the pact hasn't ended with that- for while the Gentry were bound to protect mankind, the Huntsmen were not. Bound through the stories of man and magic of fae, the once free Huntsmen were called as slaves by the new kings of the forest, to serve them and steal man's children for their own needs, and used those slaves to turn Arcadia from a vast wilderness into the magnificent realm of countless kingdoms which it is today.<br /> <br /> Where did the Gentry came from is, however, unknown. Most think they rose from the new stories humanity started to tell. Others think that they were among the first changelings who were kidnapped by the Huntsmen, which used their own gifts against their former captivators. Few whisper even darker stories, about alien gods which were discovered in castles of stones when the great Ocean which was once the Underworld has started to recess. The truth in unknown, just as the origin of the Huntsmen themselves- but one thing is certain. As it once happened, it may happen again, for better- or worse.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 06-10-2017, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T13:51:32-07:00","id":1102098,"title":"","content":"I'm also reminded of Arkham Lost, and how very fitting it is to cast &quot;Primordial Beings of the Wyrd&quot; as analogs to Old Ones/Elder Things. The Huntsman could be their abandoned and usurped servants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:12:01-07:00","id":1102137,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that be the Insatiable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T09:01:53-07:00","id":1102279,"title":"","content":"The Insatiables are, according to them, the children of a sibling of the Dark Mother, so why couldn't the Gentry be the children of another?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 06-10-2017, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:59:46-07:00","id":1102367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1101921-precursors-to-the-gentry?p=1101992#post1101992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My bet? The Huntsmen. Or at least, the poor souls the Huntsmen gathered in their &quot;Wild Hunts&quot;<br /> <br /> (in my head canon, the Huntsmen once were the ancient form of the Wyrd, horned kings and queens who lived in their hunts, treating mankind as their prey- taking the sick and the dying, the young and the old as their own. One day, soon after Father Wolf's death at the late Neolithic, humanity has started to tell new stories in order to protect themselves from the hunters- the Gentry. One community at a time, the mysterious new Fae revealed themselves before mankind, offering pledges in exchange for protection. They became the new gods of the People- the so called &quot;Lost Pantheon&quot;. They made a pact with the first people- that they will protect them from the hunters of the wilderness, and in exchange they will tell stories about them, to define and worship them. Thanks to that combined effort, the Gentry conquered the Huntsmen and made them into their own... only for humanity to discover that the pact hasn't ended with that- for while the Gentry were bound to protect mankind, the Huntsmen were not. Bound through the stories of man and magic of fae, the once free Huntsmen were called as slaves by the new kings of the forest, to serve them and steal man's children for their own needs, and used those slaves to turn Arcadia from a vast wilderness into the magnificent realm of countless kingdoms which it is today.<br /> <br /> Where did the Gentry came from is, however, unknown. Most think they rose from the new stories humanity started to tell. Others think that they were among the first changelings who were kidnapped by the Huntsmen, which used their own gifts against their former captivators. Few whisper even darker stories, about alien gods which were discovered in castles of stones when the great Ocean which was once the Underworld has started to recess. The truth in unknown, just as the origin of the Huntsmen themselves- but one thing is certain. As it once happened, it may happen again, for better- or worse.)</div> </div> </div> </div>^This is what I'd bet money on, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T11:07:27-07:00","id":1102873,"title":"","content":"As much as they shape it, the Gentry didn't create Arcadia. There were things there before them, including (good guess!) the beings they cut out the hearts of to make their Huntsmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T23:02:46-07:00","id":1103023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1101921-precursors-to-the-gentry?p=1102873#post1102873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as they shape it, the Gentry didn't create Arcadia. There were things there before them, including (good guess!) the beings they cut out the hearts of to make their Huntsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, that sounds like a potentially major shift in the origin of the Huntsmen from the preview! Colour me intrigued :P<br /> <br /> Now I must wonder (and forgive me for the Dreaming terminology) if those beings were more of a &quot;Fomorian&quot;, or a &quot;Tuatha&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T09:28:32-07:00","id":1103166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1101921-precursors-to-the-gentry?p=1103023#post1103023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, that sounds like a potentially major shift in the origin of the Huntsmen from the preview! Colour me intrigued :P<br /> <br /> Now I must wonder (and forgive me for the Dreaming terminology) if those beings were more of a &quot;Fomorian&quot;, or a &quot;Tuatha&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of the ChroD being the reconstituted remains of the Multipocalypse of the WoD. My Kerberoi are sometimes Wraiths that escaped Oblivion, my <s>Tyrants</s> Exarchs are the abstract, symbolic remains of the Mages that survived their ending, the Abyss is the remains of the now-irrelevant Consensus, the Gentry are the Faeries from Dreaming gone mad after waiting for billions of years for humans to arise anew, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 06-14-2017, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T23:24:36-07:00","id":1105961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1101921-precursors-to-the-gentry?p=1102873#post1102873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as they shape it, the Gentry didn't create Arcadia. There were things there before them, including (good guess!) the beings they cut out the hearts of to make their Huntsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>..... Oh, <i>dang</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Not Alone</b><br /> Figures and faces may be glimpsed peripherally only<br /> to disappear as they\u2019re focused on. These phantasms are<br /> called doppelgangers as they seem to mimic the viewer<br /> before dissipating. These implied and disappearing figures<br /> aren\u2019t really there but echoes carried by the dying dreams;<br /> which isn\u2019t to say a traveler is alone in the Grave Dream,<br /> she\u2019s not nearly that lucky.<br /> A handful of alien and bizarre creatures stand watch over<br /> the Dominion and the less of their attention a krewe calls to<br /> itself, the better. These creatures are ancient and aloof and<br /> few survive their prolonged attention: the Dark Man, the Hag,<br /> and the Spider. A few travelers have reported seeing large,<br /> black hounds or other monstrous images but the three figures<br /> above are the most common encounters within the Grave<br /> Dream. They may appear without warning and steal away a<br /> visitor\u2019s fear, breath, hope, or life. What\u2019s worse, fleeing back<br /> to the living world might not be enough of an escape. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Bring No Iron</b><br /> This law only pertains to those who physically travel to<br /> this Dominion through the Underworld. Changelings use<br /> this Old Law as further evidence that this dark hell has some<br /> deeper connection to their former Arcadian prisons. Despite<br /> the substantial evidence of such a connection, this Dominion<br /> remains very much an extension of the Underworld. Still, the<br /> connections are currently under investigation by at least one<br /> of the half-breed fae (see the Oneironaut below). Similar to<br /> the law before this one, the lawbreaker usually isn\u2019t confronted<br /> immediately or directly, reflecting a possible fear from the<br /> Kerberos and his kin. Still, they are patient creatures and a<br /> visitation will be upon the lawbreaker sometime soon. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Speak Not of the Cousins</b><br /> Many see or hear this rule and have no idea what<br /> it means. For those that do understand, however, they<br /> don\u2019t need to be told twice. It isn\u2019t referring to a person\u2019s<br /> familial relations but rather the very real monsters that<br /> make changelings what they are. They are the so-called<br /> Keepers, the Gentry, and the Fair Folk. They are not to be<br /> referred to, mentioned, or invoked in any way by any name.<br /> Whether they fear drawing their attention or are motivated<br /> in some other way, the Dark Man is sure to come for those<br /> that break this rule. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:37:10-07:00","id":1106100,"title":"","content":"Oooooooo...!!!<br /> <br /> ...plus, the idea Arcadia/the Hedge can and sometimes do connect to the Underworld is a nice touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:08:33-07:00","id":1106115,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the precursors to the Gentry were more akin to Beasts and the Insatiable, being the most primeval of concepts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:09:58-07:00","id":1106117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1101921-precursors-to-the-gentry?p=1102279#post1102279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Insatiables are, according to them, the children of a sibling of the Dark Mother, so why couldn't the Gentry be the children of another?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Gentry are have the Primogenitor as their father and the Dark Mother as, well, <i>mom</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T02:43:21-07:00","id":1106930,"title":"","content":"I've always wondered if all gentry were'nt human at first. If Huntsmen were the first inhabitant of Arcadia, the humans they bring with them should have been change by the Wyrd : proto-changeling, half-gobelin things, and with time Keepers. And having the raw power of humanity imagination with them, they took the power from the huntsmen and became the rulers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T09:10:51-07:00","id":1107029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arabidopsis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1101921-precursors-to-the-gentry?p=1106930#post1106930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered if all gentry were'nt human at first. If Huntsmen were the first inhabitant of Arcadia, the humans they bring with them should have been change by the Wyrd : proto-changeling, half-gobelin things, and with time Keepers. And having the raw power of humanity imagination with them, they took the power from the huntsmen and became the rulers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I think. I think that Arcadia is just pure dreamspace made manifest that used to have many a varying creatures, including what the Huntsmen used to be. And over time, humans found their way (or were hunted or stolen) for whatever reason. Some humans started to Learn more about the rules and pledges and laws that make Faerie work and over time the Wyrd changed them more and more (or they started to learn how to manipulate the wyrd via pledges and such) and eventually started to replace their own souls with titles with the end result being the First True Fae who enslaved most of the Arcadian Natives to satiate their hunger for Titles and conflict (now that they've lost their own human imagination through the process).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5